// CRYPT SHIFT — GRAVEYARD SHIFT — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CRYPT SHIFT as darksynth with industrial percussion — a game alternate of crypt,
// selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the
// live song.
// 
// A horror-film synth score run through a factory: a sixteenth-note pulse bass under
// everything, a crushed kick, a gated snare, a metal clap and Simmons toms, and the
// hook on an FM piano in octaves, the way the horror synth scores put their themes on a
// piano. The melody is crypt.js's own, bar for bar: the A phrase (A–C–B), the B phrase
// (the hook sequenced up a third), the climbing passage of bars 29–32 and the
// descending one of bars 37–40, and the Ghost Choir tune in the middle eight. A robot
// voice reads the hook in the intro and answers the choir; a razor-sync lead doubles
// the tune an octave up as the song peaks; brass stabs play chords in the hook's own
// rhythm. Then a false ending: bar 45 is a last chord and a clock, a robot says "the
// night shift never ends" (the Announcer preset on the robot throat, compiled into this
// song), the robot chant whispers the hook's head at half speed, and F major — VI in A
// minor, V in B-flat minor — turns the corner into the return, a half step up.
// 
//   1–4    intro — the pulse, a clock, the robot reading the hook (cabinet loop)
//   5–12   theme — the kit slams in; the A phrase twice on the FM piano
//   13–16  the B phrase, brass stabs
//   17–24  GHOST CHOIR — half-time on the toms, synth choir, the tune sung, the
//          robot answering; build in 23–24
//   25–28  the climb (Dm C Bm E) — razor lead, arpeggio
//   29–32  the descent (Am G F E)
//   33–40  climax — the A phrase twice, everything
//   41–44  the B phrase, into a last chord
//   45–48  FALSE ENDING — the chord, a clock, "the night shift never ends"; F major
//          turns the corner
//   49–60  THE RETURN — B-flat minor; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// WEATHER SYNC: the crypt eclipse runs on the heard song beat (CRYPT_WEATHER_TIMING,
// a 192-beat / 48-bar cycle counted from bar 1, whatever the tempo). Bars 17–24 are
// beats 64–96: the choir over the half-time toms, as the clouds cover the moon; four on
// the floor comes back at 25 as they clear. The song is 60 bars so that the next
// cycle's middle eight (bars 65–72) never comes round: the loop (5–60) ends on cycle
// beat 48, clear sky, and returns to bar 5, beat 16.
// 
// 60 bars at 112. Written by work/local/_crypt-remix-graveyard-shift.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-stops.mjs): the false ending's chord is cut on bar 46, so the clock ticks alone in dead air.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): a reverb throw on the false ending's chord (45); its room rings on over the clock.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
